{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":485796,"name":"MichaelX","username":"Surrealblend","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/surrealblend/{size}/11656_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T22:07:43.134Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI’m using the agents UI now primarily (congrats on converting me). I’m sure if i opened the IDE there’d be a bunch of stale code changes to accept.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the last several updates it’s consistently done this annoying thing where it will add a curly bracket that needs to be removed before the code can compile.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday when updating to 3.19.13, it revived an old agent that I hadn’t looked at for a week; I guess it resent the prompt and woke it up, and sort of inserted midstream from the last previous prompt (which had completed). The agent was confused, but thankfully realized it was all moot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion: 3.19.13\u003cbr\u003e\nVS Code Extension API: 1.128.0\u003cbr\u003e\nCommit: dd066f332fcea7382764400fde902f61920648d0\u003cbr\u003e\nDate: 2026-09-04T17:41:16.065Z\u003cbr\u003e\nLayout: Agent Window\u003cbr\u003e\nBuild Type: Stable\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: Default\u003cbr\u003e\nElectron: 42.10.0\u003cbr\u003e\nChromium: 148.0.7778.280\u003cbr\u003e\nNode.js: 24.18.1\u003cbr\u003e\nV8: 14.8.178.38-electron.0\u003cbr\u003e\nxterm.js: 6.1.0-beta.291\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: Darwin arm64 25.5.0\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/hqvuZpZJkHfjwuUI2DG9MN6fUWr.png?dl=1\" title=\"image\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_690x191.png\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"hqvuZpZJkHfjwuUI2DG9MN6fUWr\" width=\"690\" height=\"191\" srcset=\"https://