3e\n\u003cli\u003e…\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e…\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e…\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nWhat is meant to happen here that isn’t working correctly?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nIf applicable, attach images or videos (.jpg, .png, .gif, .mp4, .mov)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOperating System\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"48:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Windows 10/11\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"49:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e MacOS\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"50:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Linux\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eVersion Information\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor Cursor IDE: Menu → About Cursor → Copy\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor Cursor CLI: Run \u003ccode\u003eagent about\u003c/code\u003e in your terminal\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003eIDE:\nVersion: 2.xx.x\nVSCode Version: 1.105.1\nCommit: ......\n\nCLI:\nCLI Version 2026.01.17-d239e66\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nModel name (e.g., Sonnet 4, Tab…)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nRequest ID: f9a7046a-279b-47e5-ab48-6e8dc12daba1\u003cbr\u003e\nFor Background Agent issues, also post the ID: bc-…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nAdd any other context about the problem here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor?\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"87:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Yes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"88:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Sometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"89:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e No - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe more details you provide, the easier it is for us to reproduce and fix the issue. Thanks!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":2,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-07T22:07:53.728Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":7,"readers_count":6,"score":1.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170969,"topic_slug":"everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things","display_username":"system","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://cursor.com/agents","internal":false,"reflection":false,"clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":-1,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things/170969/2","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486505,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T13:50:04.338Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report and the screenshots. I can see the footer \u003ccode\u003eWorked for 149h 15m\u003c/code\u003e and the Swift file diff, that helps a lot. I’ll cover three things separately.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe agent that came back to life after the update.\u003cbr\u003e\nThat chat didn’t actually finish on our side. The \u003ccode\u003eWorked for 149h 15m\u003c/code\u003e label means the turn from September 1 was still marked as running, even though the agent had already accepted your questionnaire answer and wrote the docs. After an update, the Agents Window resumes agents it thinks were interrupted mid turn, so it re sent that response and the agent got confused for a second, but luckily realized there was nothing to do. We’re tracking this issue, the turn looks finished but is still running. I can’t share an ETA yet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWorkaround: if you see a chat like this again, the last turn has no final timestamp or a new message is just stuck in the queue, hit Stop or send a short continue message. This closes the turn, so the next restart won’t touch it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe extra \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e.\u003cbr\u003e\nI’d like to look at a specific example. Next time it happens, open the menu on the agent’s reply, choose Copy Request ID, and paste it here along with the model name you were using. Then we can see exactly what the edit returned.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChanges not accepted in the IDE.\u003cbr\u003e\nThat’s expected. Edits made in the Agents Window are already saved to disk, and the classic IDE just keeps showing them in the review tray until you accept or reject them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLet me know if the revive happens again, or if you find a Request ID for the bracket case.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T13:50:04.338Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170969,"topic_slug":"everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things/170969/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486644,"name":"MichaelX","username":"Surrealblend","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/surrealblend/{size}/11656_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T16:56:29.498Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey Dean, this is the Request ID for that continuous chat. It’s the one that resurfaced after update and when the extra curly bracket occured:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e7d12292f-69ee-42f0-92af-986c4bacc1fb\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot sure if it will be helpful though, I don’t see the file in question being edited by that agent. My sense is it’s a Cursor artifact, not a edit this agent made. Especially since it’s happened before. Next time I update I’ll see if it happens again and share the ID again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePS:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI had Grok do some digging to find when this particular code block was affected initially. Here’s the breadcrumb trail…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt was never committed. Git’s copy of that Preview has been valid the whole time. Cursor has been replaying a dirty buffer onto disk.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhat we can pin down\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLast clean local-history snapshot: Jul 23, 2026 (\u003ccode\u003eA0tj.swift\u003c/code\u003e). Preview ends correctly, no extra brace. File had no trailing newline, which makes EOF patches easy to botch.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFirst time you noticed it: Jul 31, 8:03 PM, right after a Cursor update. We already looked at this in \u003ca\u003eCursor update extra brace\u003c/a\u003e. \u003ccode\u003egit status\u003c/code\u003e was clean before the update.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFirst saved corrupt copy: Jul 31, 10:41 PM — Cursor Local History \u003ccode\u003eSZyl.swift\u003c/code\u003e, source \u003ccode\u003eUndo Create Diff\u003c/code\u003e. That’s Composer/agent apply-diff, not a typed edit. Same extra \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e after \u003ccode\u003e#Preview\u003c/code\u003e. It came back on logout/login.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSame ghost again: Aug 10 1 and Sep 7 (this chat, \u003ccode\u003eWgFM.swift\u003c/code\u003e, also \u003ccode\u003eUndo Create Diff\u003c/code\u003e).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJul 26–30 commits did touch this file (window overlays, Hide from Biomarkers) and landed clean. So the original extra \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e was almost certainly a bad agent apply that never got committed, then Cursor’s hot-exit/session restore kept writing it back after updates and logins.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e…\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd a full bug report:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTitle: Stuck session restore rewrites a clean Swift file with an extra \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e after Cursor update / logout (still happening on 3.19.13)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere: Editor / Hot Exit / Agent session restore\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBug\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter a Cursor update (and sometimes after macOS logout/login), Cursor restores a stale dirty buffer onto a file I did not edit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eLabTestDetailView.swift\u003c/code\u003e gets one extra \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e after \u003ccode\u003e#Preview\u003c/code\u003e. \u003ccode\u003egit status\u003c/code\u003e is clean before the update. After restart the file is dirty. The extra brace is never in git.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis has happened on Jul 31, Aug 10, and Sep 7 (after updating to 3.19.13). Same file, same extra \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e after \u003ccode\u003e#Preview\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJul 31 extras:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor Local History logged the rewrite as \u003ccode\u003eUndo Create Diff\u003c/code\u003e (Composer/agent apply-diff path), not a typed edit\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003estorage.json\u003c/code\u003e still pointed at a missing backup folder under \u003ccode\u003eApplication Support/Cursor/Backups/...\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePreviously closed Agent tabs also reopened — not even the most recent ones\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe file historically had no trailing newline, which makes EOF restore easy to corrupt.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot the issue: I am not leaving an uncommitted edit. Agents have \u003ccode\u003egit restore\u003c/code\u003e’d / removed the \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e several times. It comes back on the next update/login.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSteps\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClean \u003ccode\u003egit status\u003c/code\u003e on a Swift file that ends with \u003ccode\u003e#Preview { ... }\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdate Cursor and/or log out of macOS and back in\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFile shows a new uncommitted \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e after the Preview\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRevert the file, quit Cursor fully (Cmd-Q), update or re-login again → same \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e can return\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExpected: Closed Agent tabs stay closed. Files that weren’t edited are not rewritten. Missing/stale backup folders should not restore a phantom buffer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOS: macOS 26.5.2 (25F84)\u003cbr\u003e\nCursor: 3.19.13 (also saw this on 3.14.7 in July)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHappy to share Local History entry IDs (\u003ccode\u003eSZyl.swift\u003c/code\u003e Jul 31, \u003ccode\u003eWgFM.swift\u003c/code\u003e Sep 7) or the \u003ccode\u003ebackupPath\u003c/code\u003e from \u003ccode\u003estorage.json\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T16:56:29.498Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":6,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170969,"topic_slug":"everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things","display_username":"MichaelX","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":13216,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things/170969/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486764,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T18:24:53.587Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eThanks for the Request ID and the timeline. Your breakdown was spot on, and it helped close both issues.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAgent that “came back to life” after the update.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Request ID confirmed exactly what we suspected. The turn from September 1 was already finished on our side, but the Agents Window still showed it as running. So after the update relaunch, the client re-sent your questionnaire answer, and the agent correctly said there was nothing to do. This is a known issue we’re tracking. I can’t share an ETA yet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col start=\"2\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eExtra \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYour guess is right. This isn’t an edit the agent made, and it isn’t a hot exit restoring a dirty buffer. Cursor has a pending review change for \u003ccode\u003eLabTestDetailView.swift\u003c/code\u003e from an agent edit back in late July that was never accepted or rejected in the review UI. That state lives outside git, so \u003ccode\u003egit restore\u003c/code\u003e and the agent deleting the brace don’t clear it. On every relaunch, Cursor reapplies it and saves the file again, which is what shows up as \u003ccode\u003eUndo Create Diff\u003c/code\u003e in Local History. Same as what happened on August 1.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo break the loop for good:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen Cursor and find the agent chat whose review list still has \u003ccode\u003eLabTestDetailView.swift\u003c/code\u003e hanging there. It might be an old or archived chat, check those too.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick Keep or Keep All on that file. Don’t click Undo. Undo reverts the saved code, Keep only removes the review overlay.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf you can’t find it in Agents Window, open the classic editor window, open \u003ccode\u003eLabTestDetailView.swift\u003c/code\u003e, and click Keep All in the bar at the top of the file.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStart a new chat.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRun \u003ccode\u003egit restore\u003c/code\u003e on the file one more time.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter that, the \u003ccode\u003e}\u003c/code\u003e shouldn’t come back after the next update or login. If it still comes back, post your Cursor version here and we’ll dig deeper.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":11,"post_type":1,"posts_count":5,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T18:24:53.587Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":7,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":170969,"topic_slug":"everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","reply_to_user":{"id":13216,"username":"Surrealblend","name":"MichaelX","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/surrealblend/{size}/11656_2.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things/170969/11","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[485796,485797,486505,486644,486764]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1],[3,0]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":272,"name":"chat","slug":"chat"},{"id":378,"name":"agents-window","slug":"agents-window"},{"id":284,"name":"installation","slug":"installation"}],"tags_descriptions":{"agents-window":""},"fancy_title":"Everytime Cursor updates, the workspace does weird things","id":170969,"title":"Everytime Cursor updates, the workspace does weird things","posts_count":5,"created_at":"2026-09-07T22:07:43.072Z","views":55,"reply_count":2,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-08T18:24:53.587Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"everytime-cursor-updates-the-workspace-does-weird-things","category_id":6,"word_count":1736,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":13216,"featured_link":null,"pinned_globally":false,"pinned_at":null,"pinned_until":null,"image_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_1024x284.png","slow_mode_seconds":0,"draft":null,"draft_key":"topic_170969","draft_sequence":null,"unpinned":null,"pinned":false,"current_post_number":1,"highest_post_number":11,"deleted_by":null,"actions_summary":[{"id":4,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":8,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":10,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false},{"id":7,"count":0,"hidden":false,"can_act":false}],"chunk_size":20,"bookmarked":false,"topic_timer":{"id":32081,"execute_at":"2026-10-08T18:24:53.587Z","duration_minutes":43200,"based_on_last_post":true,"status_type":"close","category_id":null},"message_bus_last_id":35,"participant_count":3,"show_read_indicator":false,"thumbnails":[{"max_width":null,"max_height":null,"width":1918,"height":532,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f.png"},{"max_width":1024,"max_height":1024,"width":1024,"height":284,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_1024x284.png"},{"max_width":1000,"max_height":1000,"width":1000,"height":277,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_1000x277.png"},{"max_width":800,"max_height":800,"width":800,"height":221,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_800x221.png"},{"max_width":750,"max_height":750,"width":750,"height":208,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_750x208.png"},{"max_width":600,"max_height":600,"width":600,"height":166,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_600x166.png"},{"max_width":500,"max_height":500,"width":500,"height":138,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_500x138.png"},{"max_width":400,"max_height":400,"width":400,"height":110,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_400x110.png"},{"max_width":300,"max_height":300,"width":300,"height":83,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb102d3976271bdffd4f_2_300x83.png"},{"max_width":200,"max_height":200,"width":200,"height":55,"url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/7/a/7a240e323d6d967bc3d2fb1